#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:3 e783c6f18c3a4311bbaf230a6a7bf4c6
msgid "Templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:6 6448b009dc904fcaadb8c04991e39ec5
msgid ""
"In :doc:`Getting Started </introduction/getting-started>`, we covered the "
"distinction in Qubes OS between where you *install* your software and where "
"you *run* your software. Software that you use in most everyday tasks, is "
"installed within :term:`templates <template>`. When using Qubes OS, you "
"normally work in :term:`app qubes <app qube>`. App qubes are based on a "
"*template* qube (or more simply, just *a template*). They inherit most of "
"the `“root filesystem” <https://opensource.com/life/16/10/introduction-linux-"
"filesystems>`__, from the template. Changes you make to the root filesystem "
"are not written back to the template: if you install an application in an "
"app qube it will disappear when you shut down the qube. (You may be able to "
"work round this by using Flatpak or snap packages, which install to the "
"user’s home directory.) The user home directory *is* specific to the app "
"qube, and changes there are kept. There is a full explanation of this: :ref:"
"`user/templates/templates:inheritance and persistence`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:8 1dd304156a494b30b868d7c29caadc55
msgid ""
"If you use a :term:`Standalone <standalone>`, the **whole filesystem** is "
"specific to the standalone, and every change you make will be kept after "
"shutdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:10 7717266d0706479fbf59c6e5192a4896
msgid "The template system has significant benefits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:12 a142eeae5c604649a3ea5792e873e4f6
msgid ""
"**Security:** Each qube has read-only access to the template on which it’s "
"based, so if a qube is compromised, it cannot infect its template or any of "
"the other qubes based on that template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:14 c17660868e1b4813aeef5d55afb768dc
msgid ""
"**Storage:** Each qube based on a template uses only the disk space required "
"to store its own data (i.e., your files in its home directory), which "
"dramatically saves on disk space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:16 7245e8f739f6459891d12103cbc15a66
msgid ""
"**Speed:** It is extremely fast to create new app qubes, since the root "
"filesystem already exists in the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:18 91538058f9644951b054eb0881acbfbd
msgid ""
"**Updates:** Updates are naturally centralized, since updating a template "
"means that all qubes based on it will automatically use those updates after "
"they’re restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/templates.rst:20 df94764579f04e36a7c525fab1b19b8d
msgid ""
"An important side effect of this system is that any software installed in an "
"app qube (rather than in the template on which it is based) will disappear "
"when the app qube shuts down (see :ref:`user/templates/templates:inheritance "
"and persistence`). For this reason, we recommend installing most of your "
"software in templates, not app qubes."
msgstr ""

